# config/cloud/apps.conf.default — the TEMPLATE the installer seeds config/cloud/apps.conf from
# when that file is absent (a fresh clone has none). Copy it in place, then edit.
#
# This file holds ONLY your own extra Nextcloud apps. The installer enforces:
#   contacts                          → install&enable (always)
#   app_api (AppAPI)                  → install&disable (always)
#   spreed  (Talk)                    → install&enable (video calling on)
#   roundcube (mail webmail app)      → install&enable (mail module on)
#   notify_push (client push)         → install&enable (client push on)
# Change those from your own Nextcloud Apps page.
#
# One action per line, in order. Valid verbs: install&enable=, install&disable=,
# disable=, remove=. Multi-action form allowed: install&enable=APP_A disable=APP_B
#
# Semantics (the installer applies these against the live occ state):
#   install&enable=  install if absent, then enable. Already enabled → skip.
#   install&disable= install if absent, then disable.
#   disable=         installed app → disable it. Not installed → warns and asks.
#   remove=          installed+enabled → remove (deletes app data).
# Satisfied actions are skipped silently, so re-runs are idempotent.
